  "description": "When do mushrooms fruit in Sweden? GBIF records per month (2000–2025) for the chanterelle, funnel chanterelle, porcini, fly agaric and false morel, against all fungi. Statistics idea: months are circular, so the season's centre is a circular mean (each month an angle on the year's clock) and its length R says how concentrated the season is; records follow effort (people search in autumn), so a second mean weights each month by the species' share over all fungi's share. Beside it, Mushroom Observer's 2025 chanterelle photos with the community's identification votes: in North America the 'chanterelle' is many species. Caveats: records are presence-only and follow observers; GBIF mixes citizen science and collections; Mushroom Observer is mostly North American. Next: hover the clock for dates, click an arrow for GBIF's map, swap a taxonKey (any species from GBIF's species search) or country.",
